## Back on the island

The [browser port](https://khawkins98.github.io/johnny_web/) offers Classic and Enhanced playback. Classic keeps the native 320×200 resolution, static clouds, and flat waves; Enhanced adds responsive scaling with animated clouds and ocean waves. The original Dynamix and Sierra pixel art, audio cues, and gags remain the center of the experience.

To run it, you supply the original game data. The [README](https://github.com/khawkins98/johnny_web#readme) links the floppy archive; dropping its ZIP or extracted `.ima` disk image directly onto the page imports the resources straight into browser storage.

Like my [recent Mac OS 9 work](/posts/20260810-newsheep-sheepshaver-mac-os-9-2-apple-silicon-jit/), this started as an excuse to spend time with vintage software again. Johnny's island turned out to contain far more clever engineering than a simple screensaver had any right to have.

If you remember Johnny from back in the day, I'd love to hear which gag stuck with you. It's nice having that little castaway getting on with his life in the corner of a tab again.

